# DNS provider modules compiled into Caddy AND Matcad's import binary.
# Add more from https://github.com/caddy-dns (space-separated) and rebuild:
#   ./scripts/deploy.ps1
# Any compiled-in module can then be used via the "Custom" provider type in the UI.
CADDY_DNS_MODULES=github.com/caddy-dns/netcup github.com/caddy-dns/cloudflare github.com/caddy-dns/digitalocean github.com/caddy-dns/hetzner github.com/caddy-dns/route53 github.com/caddy-dns/gandi github.com/caddy-dns/desec github.com/caddy-dns/ovh

# Go-module replaces applied to the Caddy build (space-separated "old=new@ref" entries,
# each becomes an `xcaddy --replace`). This is how the "Netcup" (CloudDNS, new REST API)
# provider works: there is no released Caddy module for it, so we point the caddy-dns/netcup
# plugin's libdns dependency at a fork that adds REST support (it uses REST when the API
# password is empty). The fork is github.com/egs2003/libdns-netcup; we pin a fork under our
# own account for reproducibility.
#
# BEFORE THIS BUILDS: (1) fork github.com/egs2003/libdns-netcup into github.com/Real-TTX/libdns-netcup,
# (2) in the fork change go.mod's first line to `module github.com/Real-TTX/libdns-netcup` and commit
# (Go requires the module path to match the one referenced here), (3) replace the SHA below with that
# commit's SHA. Leave CADDY_DNS_REPLACES empty to build the legacy netcup module only.
CADDY_DNS_REPLACES=github.com/libdns/netcup=github.com/Real-TTX/libdns-netcup@SET_THIS_TO_YOUR_FORK_COMMIT_SHA
